      "reading": "きづいている",
      "reason": "For the general sense of 'aware' (noticing, realizing, being conscious of), '気づいている' is a much more natural and common expression in daily Japanese. Although it is a verb phrase, it functions adjectivally in context (e.g., '危険に気づいている人' - 'a person aware of the danger')."
